cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use proxy-scraper or its proxy snapshots in your work, please cite it like this."
title: "proxy-scraper: free proxies that actually work"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Feix
    given-names: Maximilian
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/maximilianfeix/proxy-scraper"
url: "https://maximilianfeix.github.io/proxy-scraper/"
abstract: >-
  proxy-scraper collects public HTTP, SOCKS4 and SOCKS5 proxies from hundreds of public lists and keeps only the
  ones that pass every check: a protocol handshake with a first request that returns a public exit IP, a second
  request to an unrelated site that shows the same exit IP, one test page that arrives byte for byte and, for HTTPS,
  a tunnel to a test host with a TLS certificate that verifies. It publishes a checked list about every hour and a
  daily snapshot with exit IP, country, ASN, datacenter flag (provider name looks like a hosting company),
  anonymity, latency, speed, share of runs on the list and site reachability.
keywords:
  - proxies
  - open proxies
  - proxy checker
  - networking
  - web scraping
